# Banding on the defending side (CR 702.22j): an attacking creature blocked by a creature with banding has its combat damage
# divided by the defending player, as they choose among the creatures blocking it - past lethal, and none of it to the
# player whatever trample would have done (CR 702.19b is the attacking player's procedure, which this replaces). Bot2's
# Ulvenwald Oddity (4/4 trample, haste) attacks; Bot1 blocks it with Benalish Hero and Guerrilla Gorilla. Bot1 puts all 4 on
# the Hero: it dies, the Gorilla is dealt nothing, and Bot1 takes nothing. Bot2 alone would have assigned 1 to the Hero, 2 to
# the Gorilla and 1 to Bot1. The Oddity is dealt 3 and lives.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Benalish Hero
Guerrilla Gorilla
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Ulvenwald Oddity
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Benalish Hero.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Guerrilla Gorilla.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Ulvenwald Oddity.Cast
Bot2.Attack(Ulvenwald Oddity > Bot1)
Bot1.Block(Benalish Hero > Ulvenwald Oddity; Guerrilla Gorilla > Ulvenwald Oddity)
[T2 Bot2.Blockers]
Bot1.AssignDamage(Ulvenwald Oddity > Benalish Hero: 4)
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 2
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Graveyard = Benalish Hero
Bot1.Battlefield.Guerrilla Gorilla.Damage = 0
Bot2.Battlefield.Ulvenwald Oddity.Damage = 3
